# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file keeps registration isolated.
# register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_graph_full_incremental_equivalence.py" "GRAPH FULL/INCREMENTAL EQUIVALENCE GATE: PASS" "full/incremental persisted graph equivalence across every extraction substrate" "For imports, calls, database tables/columns, config, Terraform, Kubernetes, GraphQL, protobuf, OpenAPI, routes, GitHub Actions/package scripts, Tauri, Celery, BullMQ, sibling stems and role features: baseline full + real incremental decision at an end commit must persist exactly the same canonical Node/Edge rows and graph_hash as an independent full build of that commit. Control fixtures also cover legal ::/angle-bracket paths, Node-ID collisions, unchanged/root/nested .gitattributes, rule changes, cg3-to-cg4 and semantic-reference-v0-to-v1 rollout, regular-file-to-symlink transitions, and ambiguous/failed baselines becoming resolved. Consumer-only resource changes must exercise patch; definition/symmetric/uncertain changes must take explicit coded full fallback. Prints per-case mode, counts, hash and a concrete persisted Edge." "DB-backed canonical graph equality and hash proof; fails on a missing resource/column edge, silent persistence loss, mixed extractor generation, stale uncertainty, unverified target-tree mode, unsafe patch, unobserved fallback or NULL telemetry" 64
